From 67e8d59acf98466e46aa14704ce774230ca288e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:57:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MTP: per-token recurrent state slots in the runner and the
 GDN layer

With speculative method "mtp", the compact GDN allocation holds one row per
token of a decode step, the runner resumes from the row of the last kept token,
and the GDN layer saves every token's state. Without it the layout and code
path are unchanged.

The slot arithmetic is tested on CPU. The speculative path has not run on HPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
